    <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">A type of Roman temple, usually found in the north-western provinces of the Roman Empire. Romano Celtic temples differ in form from rectangular Classical temples but being either square or octagonal with a central cella rising above a surrounding ambulatory.</skos:scopeNote>
