    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">CLAMP</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">A temporary structure used for the firing of bricks or tiles. Unfired bricks or tiles were stacked upon a layer of fuel (usually wood) and then surrounded by a wall of old bricks and covered by a layer of mud or clay. The clamp was then fired.</skos:scopeNote>
