    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">CLAMP LIME KILN</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">A kiln in which lime is made by calcining limestone. This type of kiln usually consists of a circular bowl surrounded by pennanular banks with a funnel exit on the lower side. They normally survive as an earthwork. Superseded by Flare Kilns.</skos:scopeNote>
